From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] StorageStatsService: do not round a size that was already decided

Settings > 存储 on V85 says 「2.80 GB（总共 4.0 GB）」 and draws 70% 已使用.
`df` on the same device says 615 MB of 1.7 GiB, 35%. The page is wrong by
1.2 GB, and wrong in the direction that tells a reader with 1.1 GiB free that
they are nearly out of room.

Patch 0020 already dealt with the cause: `getPrimaryStorageSize()` rounds the
data partition up to a power of two, for a phone whose flash chip is sold as
a round number and whose other partitions take what /data does not show.
Internal storage here is two image files on the Kindle's FAT volume -- 576 MiB
of system and 1.75 GiB of data, 2.4 GB in all -- and there is no chip size to
match, so `config_primaryStorageSizeExact` makes the method add the two and
return that.

`StorageStatsService.getTotalBytes()`, which is what Settings asks through
`StorageStatsManager`, then rounds the answer a second time: 2.4 GB goes back
up to 4.0 GB, and the donut's 「已使用」 is that minus the free space, so the
1.6 GB that does not exist is all counted as used.

The second rounding is dropped. `roundStorageSize()` returns val * pow with
val a power of two up to 512 and pow a power of 1000, and feeding such a
value back in returns it unchanged, so where `config_primaryStorageSizeExact`
is not set -- every other device -- `getPrimaryStorageSize()` has already
rounded and this returns exactly what it returned before. The other branch,
for a volume that really is a disk, is left alone.

ok
--- a/services/usage/java/com/android/server/usage/StorageStatsService.java
+++ b/services/usage/java/com/android/server/usage/StorageStatsService.java
